PART 3: cross-check against K=3 (M size 1) -- the concrete case
named in the mandate, tying back to Proposition NN3's own K=3
derivation (k3_joint_structural_attempt front, PROVED, cited).
For K=3, M = {the third source}, |M|=1, x_M =: c:
  P_same(s,s') [K=3] = x_s x_s' * (2*c + 1)
  P_disjoint(s,s') [K=3] = x_s x_s' * (2*c + 1)  (same, per identity above)
  => P_{s,s'}(K=3) = x_s x_s' * (2 + 4c) = 4*c*x_s*x_sp + 2*x_s*x_sp
  This exact per-(s,s') formula is used (via the full T(L) assembly
  in symbolic_pnn_via_composition_gf.py) to reproduce Proposition NN3
  (P_nn(n,3) = (35n^3+38n^2+23n+6)/(140n^3)) exactly -- see that
  script's own verification output for the end-to-end confirmation.
